---
description: Component-based feature architecture and code quality for this app
alwaysApply: true
---

- Build small, single-responsibility React components; route files only compose feature entry points.
- Organize independently routed features under src/features with public index.js contracts.
- Import other features only through public entry points, never their internal components.
- Keep audio, persistence, validation, data and UI in separate modules and hooks.
- Keep shared app shell, accessible primitives and providers under src/shared.
- Use feature-owned styles, configuration-driven content and responsive layouts.
- Format every supported source/config/doc file with Prettier.
- Run npm run format:check, npm run lint, npm test and npm run build before delivery.
- Keep ESLint at zero warnings; fix issues rather than suppressing rules.
- Describe single-deployment feature modules accurately; do not claim independent microfrontend deployments without implementing them.
- Never claim inquiries were delivered or dates confirmed without a working backend.
